# Ashling's Command, modes 3 and 4 in a game of three, CR 608.2b and 800.4a: Bot1 targets Bot3 for the 2 damage to each creature
# it controls and itself for two Treasures. In response Bot3, whose library is empty, casts Ancestral Recall on itself and
# loses the game; the first target is then illegal, so no damage is dealt (Bot3's Ornithopter has left with it anyway, and
# Bot2's Ornithopter, controlled by neither target, is untouched), but the second mode still resolves: Bot1 gets two Treasures.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Ashling's Command
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Ancestral Recall
Ornithopter
Island x4
Island

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot3.Main1]
Bot3.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot3.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ashling's Command.Cast
Bot1.Modes(3; 4)
Bot1.Target(Bot3)
Bot1.Target(Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot3.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot3)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot3.Status = Lost
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Ruby; Treasure Token; Treasure Token
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 0
Stack.Count = 0
